{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Naphtali, sated with favor.</b> His land is quick to ripen its fruits, and is sated from them as desired — for a place whose fruits are late does not satisfy them with desire, for one must crave them before they arrive." "<b>And full of the blessing of HaShem.</b> That everyone who comes to the land of Naphtali and sees its fruits ripening early and its trees blossoming praises and blesses HaShem for the new growth. And so Jacob said: ״הנותן אמרי שפר״. And our Rabbis expounded from here in Berakhot: whoever fills the cup of blessing merits and inherits two worlds, as it is said: ״ומלא ברכת ה׳ ים ודרום ירשה״. And there is difficulty: how are two worlds derived from here? And one may answer: ים — this is west, and this is this world, which is like night; and דרום is the place where the sun is always there, both in the days of the sun and in the days of the rains — and this is the World to Come, which is like day; and both of them are an inheritance for one who fills the cup of blessing."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:05.722994121Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}